---
source: crates/api/tests/edits.rs
expression: request.instruction
---
Edit the first image. The second image is the same photo with a bright magenta outline drawn around the couch; that outline is the new silhouette the couch must have. First work out what the couch actually is (what kind of object, what it is made of, how it is built), then reshape it the way a real couch of that kind could look in this shape: keep its material, thickness, the proportions of its parts, edges, reflections, highlights, shadows and perspective physically believable, so the result looks like an untouched photograph of a real object, not an edited or distorted picture. Make the outer edge follow the magenta line exactly, and redraw whatever the old shape covered or the new shape uncovers so it looks natural. The magenta marks are guides only: do not draw them in the result. Everything outside the reshaped couch must stay identical to the original. Output only the full edited image with the same framing and aspect ratio as the original.
